{
  "_comment": [
    "The photographs behind AthenIQ's course cards.",
    "",
    "One pool per *subject*, not one per course: a program is thirty or forty",
    "courses that share a handful of subjects, and a wall of near-identical stock",
    "photographs is worse than a smaller, better-chosen set. `scripts/course-photos.py`",
    "resolves a course to a subject by its title, then picks a photograph from that",
    "subject's pool with a hash of the course key, so the choice is stable across",
    "runs and neighbouring courses do not repeat.",
    "",
    "The images are committed under",
    "`contrib/atheniq-theme/lms/static/images/courses/` and are served by the LMS",
    "as `/static/atheniq/images/courses/<file>`, which is what",
    "`publish-courses.py` writes into each course's `course_image_url`.",
    "",
    "Source: Unsplash (https://unsplash.com/license) \u2014 free for commercial and",
    "non-commercial use, no permission or attribution required. Each entry is an",
    "`images.unsplash.com` photo id; `make course-photos` re-fetches them at",
    "1200x675.",
    "",
    "Adding a subject: add the pool here and a few keywords. Adding a course:",
    "nothing \u2014 it resolves from its title. `make course-photos -- --list` shows",
    "the mapping for every course in the tree."
  ],
